excess value, whether deficits are safely bounded, and whether liquidation can 
be forced to revert or leave inconsistent balances. This complements the 
completed LiquidateCurrencyAction review without repeating it, because the 
underlying library implementation and invariants remain unexamined. EXIT 
CRITERIA: Trace every liquidation calculation and state-mutating helper used by 
the library; verify requested amounts, liquidity-token values, collateral 
withdrawals, caps, rounding, and deficit handling across zero, maximum, and 
insolvency cases; confirm authorization and caller assumptions; document any 
exploitable issue or conclude that all relevant invariants are preserved.

